Date: Fri, 24 Jul 2026 19:11:59 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 126/143] drm/sun4i: sun55i_de: drop the inert alpha property
 from the RCQ primary

The multi-plane hardening removed the plane-alpha property from the
LAY1..3 overlay planes because the hardware ignores it there, but the
RCQ primary kept it while being just as inert: the staging always
programs the layer with global alpha 0xff (sun55i_de_layer_update) and
blender pipe 0 has no per-pipe alpha/premul (vendor note quoted in the
cursor commit), so a userspace-set alpha value changes nothing on
screen.

Advertising a property the hardware never applies is the same UAPI lie
the overlay hardening fixed; stop creating it on the RCQ primary.  The
non-RCQ (DE2/DE3) primaries keep the property - their backend really
applies it.  No register programming changes.

Co-Authored-By: AI Agent
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/sun4i/sun8i_ui_layer.c | 17 +++++++++++++----
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/sun4i/sun8i_ui_layer.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/sun4i/sun8i_ui_layer.c
index f5fd2b157..378c8e964 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/sun4i/sun8i_ui_layer.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/sun4i/sun8i_ui_layer.c
@@ -684,10 +684,19 @@ struct sun8i_layer *sun8i_ui_layer_init_one(struct drm_device *drm,
 
 	plane_cnt = mixer->cfg->ui_num + mixer->cfg->vi_num;
 
-	ret = drm_plane_create_alpha_property(&layer->plane);
-	if (ret) {
-		dev_err(drm->dev, "Couldn't add alpha property\n");
-		return ERR_PTR(ret);
+	/*
+	 * No plane-alpha property on the v35x RCQ primary: the staging always
+	 * programs the layer opaque (global alpha 0xff) and blender pipe 0 has
+	 * no per-pipe alpha/premul (vendor note), so the property would
+	 * advertise a translucency the hardware never applies - same reasoning
+	 * that keeps it off the LAY1..3 overlay planes.
+	 */
+	if (!mixer->cfg->uses_rcq) {
+		ret = drm_plane_create_alpha_property(&layer->plane);
+		if (ret) {
+			dev_err(drm->dev, "Couldn't add alpha property\n");
+			return ERR_PTR(ret);
+		}
 	}
 
 	/*
